                     <origDate notBefore="1400" notAfter="1800" evidence="lettering" cert="medium">The manuscript consists of two codicological units. 
                        The fragment referred to as <ref target="#p1"/> originates from a different, older, and larger manuscript dating to the 15th century. It is a singleton 
                        with a stub, <locus target="#1"/>, which belongs to <ref target="#q1"/> and serves as an endleaf.
                       Owing to its large size, it was inserted sideways on the right, so the text appears perpendicular to the main writing surface.  
                        The unit referred to as <ref target="#p2"/> can be dated to the 18th century. 
                        </origDate>
