                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus target="#153v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">Excerpt from <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3509Epistle">1 Joh. 1</title>; it is written in a very crude hand. Possibly it is a writing
                              exercise of a certain <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15344ZawaldaMar">Zawalda Māryām</persName>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"/>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#169vb"/>
                           <desc type="OwnershipNote">Ownership note written in <ref target="#h2">Hand 2</ref>. The name of the owner has been erased.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"/>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a4">
                           <locus from="170ra" to="171rb"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3108RepCh388">Yǝweddǝsǝwwa malāʾǝkt la-Māryām</title>;  the prayer has been written in a mediocre hand. The initial line and the name of St Mary are rubricated.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"/>
                        </item>
                        
                       
                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <locus target="#68v"/>
                           <desc>The midpoint of the <ref target="#ms_i1.1">‘Psalms of David’</ref> (in Psalm 76).</desc> 
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e5">
                        <desc>The Psalms are divided into groups of ten separated by a line of alternating black and red dots.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e6">
                           <locus target="#2r #3r #5r #7r #17v #21v #36r #76r #77r #107v #117v #142ar #144"/>
                           <desc>The scribe reduced the size of his handwriting to accommodate the
                              end of the line. The folia listed above are a few examples.</desc>
                        </item>
                           
                        <item xml:id="e7">
                           <locus target="#21v #22v #31v #87v #102v #107v #116v #126v #135r #142r"/>
                           <desc>Part of the line is taken up.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e8">
                           <locus target="#89v"/>
                           <desc>Part of the line is taken down.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e9">
                           <locus target="#152r15"/> 
                           <desc type="Correction">Tamallas-sign indicating where the omission belongs.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e10">
                           <locus target="#2r #32r #39r #40r #40v #41r #58v #67v #68r #87r #89r #90v #91v #100r #104r #117r #125r #142ar #148v #149rv #150rv #151r #152r #153r"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Omitted words and passages are written interlineally and in the margins, in the main hand and in a secondary hand.</desc> 
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e11">
                           <locus target="#15r #52r #66v #109v #110r #114r #142r"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Corrections over erasures, in the main and in secondary hands.</desc> 
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e12">
                           <locus from="147r" to="153r"/>
                           <desc type="Correction"><ref target="#p2_i1.3"/> contains numerous corrections.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e13">
                           <locus target="#32r #52v"/>
                           <desc type="Correction">Erasures.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e14">
                           <locus target="#82r"/>
                           <desc>Pen trials.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e15">
                           <locus target="#2r  #81v #89v #90r #99r #113v #115v #137v #143r #171rb #170v"/>
                           <desc>Scribbling, doodles.</desc>
                        </item>
                       
                        <item xml:id="e16">
                           <locus target="#90r"/>
                           <desc>The title of Psalm 101 <foreign xml:lang="gez">ጸሎተ፡ ባሕታዊ፡</foreign> is written in the upper margin.</desc>
                        </item>
                     </list>
                  </additions>
                        </physDesc>
